*---------------------- EXTENDED HEADER FIELD
* The `3x` / `4x` channel families are "invisible" (hidden) keysound objects:
* they belong to a lane and play through the key bus, but they are never drawn
* and never judged. Chart authors use them to keep a lane's sample assignment
* alive across a section where no note should be hit.
*
* Two properties are only observable from a whole chart, which is why this
* fixture exists next to the channel-classifier unit tests:
*
*   - invisible channels are play-lane SOUND channels but not PLAYABLE ones, so
*     they must not contribute a judged note
*   - they must not influence lane-mode detection either: the 2P-side `4x`
*     channels below must not turn this single-player chart into a DP chart
*
* Visible lanes are `11..13` plus `18` / `19`, so the expected lane mode is
* 7 KEY SP.

#PLAYER 1
#LNTYPE 1

